@startuml architecture
' Architecture: one app, two terminals and two storages.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 42

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
    BorderColor #4A6FA5
    ArrowColor #4A6FA5
    HeaderBackgroundColor #DCE6F2
    FontSize 13
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
    BorderColor #C9A227
    FontSize 12
}

package "Desktop (JVM)" #EAF6EA {
    class Main <<entry point>> {
        + main(args)
        - new ConsoleTerminal()
        - new FileStorage(path)
    }
    class FileStorage {
        + readLines()
        + writeLines(lines)
    }
    class DataDirectory <<platform data dir>> {
        + collectionFile() : Path
    }
}

package "Browser (WebAssembly)" #FDF0E6 {
    class BrowserMain <<entry point>> {
        + main(args)
        - new WebTerminal()
        - new LocalStorageStorage(key)
    }
    class WebInput <<JS bridge>> {
        + deliverLine(line)
        + closeInput()
    }
    class WebTerminal {
        + readLine()  {coroutine}
    }
    class LocalStorageStorage {
        + readLines()
        + writeLines(lines)
    }
}

class FilmSamlingApp <<program>> {
    + run()
}

interface Terminal <<interface>> {
    + readLine() : String
    + println(line)
    + print(text)
    + printf(format, args...)
}

interface Storage <<interface>> {
    + readLines() : List<String>
    + writeLines(lines)
    + exists() : boolean
    + clear()
}

class ConsoleTerminal {
    + readLine()
}

Main --> ConsoleTerminal : creates
Main --> FileStorage : creates
Main --> DataDirectory : resolves the path with
Main --> FilmSamlingApp : runs
BrowserMain --> WebTerminal : creates
BrowserMain --> LocalStorageStorage : creates
BrowserMain --> FilmSamlingApp : runs
ConsoleTerminal ..|> Terminal
WebTerminal ..|> Terminal
FileStorage ..|> Storage
LocalStorageStorage ..|> Storage
FilmSamlingApp o--> Terminal : uses only these
FilmSamlingApp o--> Storage : uses only these
WebTerminal --> WebInput : waits for lines
WebInput ..> WebTerminal : resumes with a line
FileStorage --> File : "the collection file"
LocalStorageStorage --> LocalStorage : localStorage

class File <<java.io>> {
    films.csv in the
    per-user data dir
}
class LocalStorage <<browser>> {
    localStorage
}

note bottom of FilmSamlingApp
  The program never mentions Scanner,
  System.in, System.out, File or
  localStorage. It knows only the
  Terminal and Storage interfaces.
end note

note bottom of DataDirectory
  ~/.local/share/filmsamling on Linux
  (or $XDG_DATA_HOME), %APPDATA% on
  Windows, ~/Library/Application Support
  on macOS. Runtime data, so it stays out
  of the project and survives a clean build.
end note

note right of WebTerminal
  readLine() compiles to a coroutine:
  it suspends instead of blocking
  the browser's single thread.
end note

note bottom of LocalStorageStorage
  TeaVM does provide java.io.File in the
  browser, but it lives in memory and is
  lost on reload, so localStorage is used
  instead. The collection never silently
  disappears.
end note
@enduml
